    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c2_figurative_language_cleft_sentences",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-figurative-language-01",
        "slug": "c2-figurative-language-cleft-sentences",
        "title": "Cleft sentences for focus",
        "rule_summary": "Use what-clauses and it-clefts to place deliberate emphasis on the most important part of a message.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "با what-clause و it-cleft بخش مهم پیام را برجسته می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "What concerns me most is the lack of independent oversight.",
            "fa": "چیزی که بیشتر نگرانم می‌کند نبود نظارت مستقل است."
          },
          {
            "en": "It was the timing, rather than the decision itself, that caused the problem.",
            "fa": "زمان‌بندی بود، نه خود تصمیم، که مشکل را ایجاد کرد."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c2_figurative_language_cohesion_reference",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-figurative-language-02",
        "slug": "c2-figurative-language-cohesion-reference",
        "title": "Cohesion through reference",
        "rule_summary": "Use this, such, the former/latter, these findings, and related reference devices so longer discourse remains connected without repetition.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "با this، such، the former/latter، these findings و ابزارهای ارجاعی مشابه، متن یا گفتار طولانی را بدون تکرار منسجم نگه می‌داریم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "The first approach is cheaper; the latter, however, is easier to scale.",
            "fa": "رویکرد اول ارزان‌تر است؛ اما دومی مقیاس‌پذیرتر است."
          },
          {
            "en": "These findings raise a further question about access.",
            "fa": "این یافته‌ها پرسش دیگری درباره دسترسی مطرح می‌کنند."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c2_figurative_language_advanced_hedging",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-figurative-language-03",
        "slug": "c2-figurative-language-advanced-hedging",
        "title": "Advanced hedging and calibration",
        "rule_summary": "Calibrate certainty with expressions such as arguably, broadly speaking, tends to, appears to, and cannot entirely be ruled out.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "در C1 میزان قطعیت را با عبارت‌هایی مثل arguably، broadly speaking، tends to، appears to و cannot entirely be ruled out دقیق تنظیم می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "The change appears to have improved access, although the evidence is still limited.",
            "fa": "به نظر می‌رسد این تغییر دسترسی را بهتر کرده، هرچند شواهد هنوز محدود است."
          },
          {
            "en": "That explanation cannot entirely be ruled out.",
            "fa": "نمی‌توان آن توضیح را کاملاً منتفی دانست."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c2_figurative_language_scene_1",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-figurative-language-01",
        "title": "Figurative Language, Connotation & Conceptual Metaphor: part 1",
        "setting": "quiet cafe",
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "simple-messages",
        "characters": [
          "Nora",
          "Samir"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Nora",
            "text": "What is the practical implication of that point?",
            "translation_fa": "پیامد عملی اون نکته چیه؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "Samir",
            "text": "Calling the reform a 'bridge' frames it as a temporary connection between two states rather than a destination in itself.",
            "translation_fa": "اینکه اصلاحات رو bridge بنامیم اون رو به‌عنوان اتصال موقت بین دو وضعیت قاب‌بندی می‌کنه نه مقصد نهایی."
          },
          {
            "order": 3,
            "speaker": "Nora",
            "text": "Does the evidence justify going that far?",
            "translation_fa": "آیا شواهد واقعاً چنین نتیجه‌ای رو توجیه می‌کنه؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 4,
            "speaker": "Samir",
            "text": "A literal paraphrase preserves the basic information but often loses the emotional and evaluative work done by the original image.",
            "translation_fa": "بازگویی لفظی اطلاعات اصلی رو نگه می‌داره ولی اغلب کار احساسی و ارزشی تصویر اصلی رو از دست می‌ده."
          }
        ],
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
